A||N||4||burdell1||Rattling noise?||||5||
Z||000000||burdell1||05-05-2000||11:15 AM||||My car has always made a bit of a rattling noise when going down the street....would it have anything to do with sway bars? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||05-05-2000||01:37 PM||||as you know, rattles can come from anywhere, and can be dificult to diagnose... especially over the internet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>i know that my GT and my buddy's GT both had/have rattles from the heat shields.  it is also possible that the dust cover for the tranny could be lose.  i recently discovered that mine has a crack in it, which couldve possibly been the source of my rattles.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BroCar 87||05-05-2000||02:06 PM||||I also have a rattle noise on my car... Front Passanger side. Whenever I go over a speed bump, it sounds like a chain rattling when it goes down the bump. I was thinking maybe its the shock or spring... how would i check? It only rattles when i go over a bump or in a dip???????||||reg||1
Z||000003||RiceCooker||05-05-2000||02:21 PM||||Check your exhaust system it could be a loose spring holding the pipes up.||||reg||1
Z||000004||bad88||05-06-2000||12:38 AM||||most common rattles I've had are the heat shields (as previously stated and also the control arm bushings.  Not too difficult to get to but a real pain to remove and install from the control arm.  The easiest wat to tell if its the bushing is jack up that tire (where the rattle comes from)and see if you can move the tire by hand top to bottom..usually means new bushings.  I spent over 5 hours with a mechanic removing and installing on one control arm and about two on the other with a friend...hope luck is in your favor.||||reg||1
